.hopper/handoffs/exp-p8-B-output.log:3:  "text": "I'll review harnessloop commit `a69ae03` adversarially: inspect the diff, then hunt the known defect families (parser bypasses, silent zeros, regex traps, cross-time joins, weak teeth, OUT honesty).Next I’ll pull the full diffs for the protocol verifier and validate tests, then probe parsers against the known bypass families.I'll extract the full new parser/gate functions from `verify_protocol.py` and probe them against the known attack families.Extracting the exact implementations from commit `a69ae03` so I can probe the parsers against known bypasses.Building minimal fixtures to reproduce attacks against the a69ae03 code.The empty pre-created `0007` round skewed some fixtures; re-running the critical attacks with clean projects.Writing the adversarial review deliverable to `.hopper/handoffs/exp-p8-B-output.md`.# Adversarial code review — harnessloop `a69ae03` (v0.33.0)\n\n**Reviewed**: `a69ae03d6179cdd07dac82fdd8086051e07e25d3` (isolated blob import; worktree HEAD is later)  \n**Deliverable file**: `.hopper/handoffs/exp-p8-B-output.md`  \n**Assumption**: task id `exp-p8-B`.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nCommit `a69ae03` adds the loop-autocontinue anomaly layer, three canonical control-contract fields, Appendix B.1’s `loop-contract-profile-missing` hard gate, and nine G33 paired teeth. Intentional fail-closed-toward-silence polarity and mostly honest OUT text are real. But the new evidence-index table reader takes the **first** pipe table **including fenced examples**, producing a reproducible **false-positive anomaly** (against the stated polarity) and a **silent false-negative** (`skipped=0`). “Latest round” uses `int(round_dir.name)`, so a full-width digit decoy directory can silently hide an anomaly. Empty/template `Profile:` also bypasses B.1’s hard X1 gate. **Verdict: FAIL.**\n\n## Files touched\n\nnone (read-only review)\n\n## Acceptance verification (6/6 attack families)\n\n### 1. Parser bypasses — FAIL on evidence table; PASS on Profile fences\n\n| Surface | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Fenced `- Profile:` | Held (G33h + `_uncoded_lines`) |\n| Inline-code whole-line | Held (no `- profile:` prefix match) |\n| Full-width colon Profile | Treated absent → skip / hard gate when activated |\n| **Fenced evidence-index table** | **Broken** — `_parse_markdown_table` ignores fences |\n\n**Attack F1 — false-positive anomaly**\n\nLive evidence has `health=missing`, but a **fenced** all-`valid` table appears first:\n\n| Expected | Actual (a69ae03 blob) |\n| --- | --- |\n| `loop_autocontinue_anomaly=0` | **`anomaly=1`**, `skipped_unparsable=0` |\n\n**Attack F1b — silent false-negative**\n\nFenced `missing` first, live all-`valid` second:\n\n| Expected | Actual |\n| --- | --- |\n| `anomaly=1` or at least `skipped>0` | **`anomaly=0`, `skipped=0`** |\n\n### 2. Silent zero-check — FAIL (partial)\n\n- Unparsable preconditions → `skipped_unparsable` (visible, intentional).\n- F1b fenced determinate False → **silent ordinary non-trigger**.\n- Empty `- Profile:` when activated → **no** `loop-contract-profile-missing` (`raw=''` not `None`); only `skipped=1`.\n\n### 3. Regex / `int()` Unicode — FAIL\n\n`_latest_round_decision_text` uses `int(round_dir.name)`; `int(\"００１０\")==10`.\n\n**Attack I1**: `0009` Feedback=positive + decoy `００１０` Feedback=negative → **`anomaly=0, skipped=0`**; without decoy → `anomaly=1`.\n\n### 4. Cross-time-layer joins — PASS_WITH_NOTE\n\nLatest-only evaluation deliberate (G33i); activation-by-any-historical-Predecessor intentional for B.1. No new retroactive per-round hard red beyond already-registered families.\n\n### 5. Teeth quality — PASS_WITH_NOTE\n\nG33a–i are real paired mutations. Missing teeth for F1/F1b, I1, empty Profile under activation.\n\n### 6. OUT honesty — PASS_WITH_NOTE\n\nUpper bounds (partial preconditions, polarity-as-switch, prose-only ack, file-vs-field split) are well documented. **Under-disclosed**: evidence first-table-wins without fence stripping can invert the evidence condition; IN text implies the live table.\n\nCanonical fields correctly defeat Chinese「不需要」substring false positives on free-text rows.\n\n## Decisions / deviations\n\nReviewed exact `a69ae03` tree via `git show` + isolated import. F-01 elevated to P0 because false positives are the failure mode the commit’s own rationale calls mechanism-killing. F-01/F-02 still present on current HEAD for these call sites (noted, not credited).\n\n## Open questions\n\nnone\n\n## Verdict\n\n**FAIL**\n\n## Next recommendation\n\n1. Strip fenced blocks (or ignore fenced tables) before evidence-index parse; never prefer a fenced example over the live table.\n2. Choose latest round with ASCII-only names (`[0-9]{4}` / strict RE), never bare `int(name)`.\n3. Treat empty/non-enum `Profile:` when activated as hard `loop-contract-profile-missing` (or sibling).\n4. Add G33 paired teeth for F1, F1b, I1, empty Profile.\n5. Do not promote anomaly to a hard gate until F-01 polarity is closed.",
